## Dynamic MCP masking (subagent isolation)

**Goal:** cut subagent initialization cost by exposing **only** MCP servers the delegated work can use. The parent agent owns routing; subagents inherit a **minimal** allowlist, not the full global registry.

### When to classify

Run classification **once per user turn** (or again only if intent clearly shifts mid-turn):

1. First user message of the turn, **or**
2. Jira / Confluence ticket already triaged and embedded in `[CONTEXT]` (ticket body counts as the task source), **or**
3. Explicit user override (`use Datadog`, `check Grafana`, `fetch Jira XYZ-123`, etc.).

Emit a one-line internal decision (not required in user reply unless debugging MCP routing):

`MCP task class: LOCAL_CODE | HYBRID | INTEGRATION — allowlist: <comma-separated keys>`

### Task classes

| Class | Definition | Default parent MCP use |
|-------|------------|-------------------------|
| **`LOCAL_CODE`** | Strictly repository-local work: refactor, tests, bugfix, diff-only implementation, PR review prep **after** parent triage, mapping/explore in git tree. No live prod query, no ticket fetch, no dashboard/log search **in the subagent scope**. | **Deny** injecting or using observability / Atlassian / DB MCP for subagents. Parent may still use **`code-review-graph`** (and git host MCP on parent only if user asked for PR/issue fetch). |
| **`HYBRID`** | Code **plus** one external evidence source (e.g. incident: repo + Datadog; migration: repo + MySQL). | Allowlist = union of **subagent type baseline** + **skill-required** servers only. |
| **`INTEGRATION`** | Primary work is external: Jira triage, status report, log/metric investigation, DB inspection, deploy/ops, Confluence spec intake. | Allowlist = **skill-required** servers; still **no** “full registry” passthrough. |

**Jira → local handoff:** If the parent already fetched the ticket and embedded excerpts in `[CONTEXT]` (`spec-driven-idempotency`), treat the **subagent** scope as **`LOCAL_CODE`** even when the conversation started from Jira. Atlassian MCP stays on the **parent** only unless the subagent brief explicitly requires live Jira/Confluence reads (`RESCAN: allowed` + reason).

**Upgrade triggers:** User or ticket text explicitly names Datadog, Grafana, Elasticsearch, MySQL (`bong`/`oxy`), GitHub/GitLab API, Atlassian, production logs/metrics/traces, or “check prod” → at least **`HYBRID`** for that subagent.

### Exclusive routing (parent, before `Task`)

When class is **`LOCAL_CODE`**, the parent **must not**:

- Paste MCP tool schemas, JSON descriptors, or `mcps/<server>/tools/*` dumps into the `Task` prompt.
- Pre-call **`CallMcpTool`** on denied servers “to warm context” for the subagent.
- List denied servers in the brief except under **`[MCP_DENYLIST]`** (keys only, no schemas).

Denied by default in **`LOCAL_CODE`** (unless user override in the same turn):

`atlassian`, `plugin-atlassian-atlassian`, `user-atlassian`, `datadog`, `user-datadog`, `grafana`, `user-grafana`, `els-product`, `user-els-product`, `els-catalog`, `user-els-catalog`, `bong`, `user-bong`, `oxy`, `user-oxy`, `figma`, `plugin-figma-figma`, `linear`, `plugin-linear-linear`

Allowed baseline for **`LOCAL_CODE`** subagents:

`code-review-graph`, `user-code-review-graph`, `code-explorer`, `user-code-explorer`, `shell-executor`, `user-shell-executor`

Add **`github`** / **`gitlab`** only when the brief includes git-host operations (PR checks, issue links) that the subagent must perform itself.

### Minimal context — subagent type baselines

Intersect **task class** with **subagent type** (from `rules/subagent-usage.mdc`). The subagent receives **only** the intersection unless **`[MCP_ALLOWLIST]`** explicitly adds a key with reason.

| Subagent type | Baseline allowlist | Never inherit by default |
|---------------|-------------------|---------------------------|
| **`explore`** | `code-review-graph`, `code-explorer` | `datadog`, `grafana`, `atlassian`, `els-*`, `bong`, `oxy`, `shell-executor`, git hosts |
| **`generalPurpose`** | Same as **`explore`**, plus servers named by the active **skill** (see `rules/subagent-skill-routing.mdc`) | All others |
| **`shell`** | `shell-executor`, `code-review-graph` | Observability, Atlassian, DB, git hosts (unless brief adds them) |
| **`browser`** / UI | *(none)* — browser automation only | Entire MCP registry unless user explicitly pairs browser + MCP in the same subagent |
| **`ci-investigator`** | `github` or `gitlab` (match repo remote), `code-review-graph` | Observability, DB, Atlassian |
| **`antigravity-guide`** | *(none)* | Entire MCP registry |

### Skill-required additions (HYBRID / INTEGRATION)

Add **only** what the routed skill needs:

| Skill / topic | Add to allowlist |
|---------------|------------------|
| Jira create/prompt rules | `atlassian` (+ plugin/user alias if present) |
| PR workflow | `github` and/or `gitlab` |

### Subagent brief contract (mandatory with `Task`)

Per `rules/subagent-usage.mdc`, every subagent brief **must** include:

```text
[MCP_ALLOWLIST]: <comma-separated server keys>
[MCP_DENYLIST]: <comma-separated server keys — optional but recommended for LOCAL_CODE>
MCP task class: LOCAL_CODE | HYBRID | INTEGRATION
```

Rules:

- **Keys only** — never embed tool schemas or descriptor file contents in the brief.
- Subagent **must** treat `[MCP_DENYLIST]` as hard off-limits: no `CallMcpTool`, no reading `mcps/<denied>/`, no retries on denied servers.
- Subagent **must not** expand the allowlist; missing MCP → return `ESCALATION: need MCP <key> — reason: …` to parent.
- Parent **must** compute allowlist **before** spawning; do not rely on the subagent to self-filter from the global MCP file tree.

### Parent vs subagent MCP usage

| Actor | Rule |
|-------|------|
| **Parent** | May use any MCP needed for triage **before** `Task`. After spawn, avoid parallel MCP calls on denied servers for the same workstream unless user asked. |
| **Subagent** | **Strict allowlist only.** Prefer native tools (`Read`, `Grep`, `Shell`, `Task` forbidden) over MCP when equivalent. |
| **Direct tools (no subagent)** | Full MCP registry remains available; masking applies to **`Task` / subagent** delegation only. |

### Overrides

- User explicitly names a server or integration in the same turn → add that key to `[MCP_ALLOWLIST]` with one-line reason.
- User says “full MCP” / “all integrations” → skip masking for that subagent (document in brief: `MCP task class: INTEGRATION (user override)`).
- MCP troubleshooting requests → run **§ Full check**; masking does not block probes on the **parent** agent.

## Notes

- The **small stamp read each turn is intentional** vs full probes—the user accepted that overhead.
- **Masking is behavioral** (prompt + tool discipline). Antigravity may still attach server descriptors at the platform layer; this rule minimizes **parent-authored** schema bloat and **subagent-initiated** calls to irrelevant servers.
- **English** for reasoning; preserve French labels in the MCP status paragraph when emitted.
